Author: Tian Pan <puncsky@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 31 20:58:48 2026 -0700

    fix(ci): pre-download the Trivy DB with per-repo retries before the CVE scans
    
    Fixes red main run 41254794386: the operator report scan stalled on the
    GHCR trivy-db transfer until Trivy's single 5m timeout expired, so the
    GCR mirror listed after it was never tried. A setup step now fetches the
    DB once with a 2m per-attempt timeout, alternating GHCR and GCR for three
    rounds, then the ten scans skip their own DB update. The five blocking
    CRITICAL gates are unchanged.

diff --git a/.github/workflows/deploy.yml b/.github/workflows/deploy.yml
index 43edff380..be8550381 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/deploy.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/deploy.yml
@@ -341,6 +341,32 @@ jobs:
           done
 
       # --- 1f. CVE scan: CRITICAL fails CI, HIGH warns (w7/m10 t001) ---
+      # Fetch the vulnerability DB once, before the ten scans, with a short
+      # per-attempt timeout that alternates GHCR and the GCR mirror. Trivy's
+      # own download shares one 5m --timeout across every repository, so a
+      # stalled GHCR transfer used it all and the mirror was never tried
+      # (run 41254794386). Each scan then reads the job-local DB as is.
+      - uses: aquasecurity/setup-trivy@3fb12ec12f41e471780db15c232d5dd185dcb514 # v0.2.6
+        with:
+          version: v0.70.0
+          cache: false
+      - name: CVE scan — download the vulnerability DB (retried)
+        env:
+          TRIVY_CACHE_DIR: ${{ github.workspace }}/.cache/trivy
+        run: |
+          for attempt in 1 2 3; do
+            for repo in ${TRIVY_DB_REPOSITORY//,/ }; do
+              if trivy image --download-db-only --db-repository "$repo" --timeout 2m; then
+                echo "TRIVY_SKIP_DB_UPDATE=true" >> "$GITHUB_ENV"
+                exit 0
+              fi
+              echo "::warning::Trivy DB download from $repo failed (attempt $attempt)"
+            done
+            sleep 10
+          done
+          echo "::error::Trivy DB unavailable from every repository after 3 rounds"
+          exit 1
+
       # Trivy scans both built+pushed images for known CVEs. Two passes per image:
       # a non-blocking HIGH+CRITICAL report (always exits 0, shows the full picture)
       # and a blocking CRITICAL-only gate (exit-code 1 if any CRITICAL is found).
